---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import ToolArtwork from '../components/ToolArtwork.astro';
---
<Base>
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="hero frame" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">A few useful tools, at home on your Mac.</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Small tasks.<span>Less friction.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">Create a file. Prepare an image. Open a link.<br class="wide-break"/> The little things, right where you need them.</p>
      <ToolArtwork/>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="air-button air-button--primary" href="#download"><Icon name="download" size={18}/>Get CloakTools</a><a class="air-button air-button--quiet" href="#product">Explore features <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></a></div>
      <p class="availability">macOS 27 or later · Apple silicon only<span>Free · Public beta</span></p>
    </section>
    <section id="product" class="section frame" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="product-title">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A little help, close at hand</p><h2 id="product-title">Make something.<br/>Keep moving.</h2><p>Start a file from Finder, keep your own templates close, turn an image into a ready-to-use copy, or give a link the right place to open. Small actions with familiar Mac controls.</p></div>
      <figure class="product-preview"><picture><source media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" srcset="/images/workbench-dark.png"/><img src="/images/workbench-light.png" width="2000" height="1400" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Finder Tools grouped by what is selected: folders, files or an image. Actions include comparing folders, collecting copies and reading a QR code."/></picture><figcaption>Finder Tools in the upcoming beta, with actions grouped by what you select.</figcaption></figure>
      <div class="features">
        <article><p class="eyebrow">A fresh start</p><h3>A new file, right here.</h3><p>Create text, Markdown and PDF files. Keep templates and folder presets close, or save what you copied. Create or read a QR code, clean up text or collect notes into a Markdown digest. Optional Developer Tools adds JSON, Base64, sample files and 13 programming languages.</p></article>
        <article><p class="eyebrow">Ready to use</p><h3>A copy of its own.</h3><p>Fit an image within a size and dimension limit, export video or audio, or save a reviewed file list. Reuse your usual export settings. Image conversion and PDF tools stay close when needed. Preview each action and keep your originals untouched.</p></article>
        <article><p class="eyebrow">The right destination</p><h3>A choice for every link.</h3><p>Pin your browsers and mail apps, choose a fallback, or make a rule for recurring links. Test the match privately before opening anything. Set up web and email handling separately, and restore your previous apps when you choose.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="provenance" class="section frame" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="craft-title">
      <div class="craft-grid"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Made with care</p><h2 id="craft-title">Useful tools.<br/>Thoughtful details.</h2><p>Ordinary files in Finder. Clear choices on your Mac. A toolkit that stays small and works without an account.</p></div><div class="principles">
        <article><h3>At home on your Mac.</h3><p>Native settings, keyboard controls and compact Liquid Glass dialogs. Optional Open After Creation opens text in TextEdit and PDFs or clipboard images in Preview.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Your work, preserved.</h3><p>Existing files are never replaced. Saved templates keep their own content. Each action uses the settings it started with, so later changes don’t alter work in progress.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Better, together.</h3><p>Part of Cloakyard, alongside CloakDrop and CloakRoll. Familiar controls, local processing and a shared attention to detail. Save templates, presets and export recipes for the tasks you come back to.</p><a class="text-link" href="/source/">See what’s being built <Icon name="link" size={16}/></a></article>
      </div></div>
    </section>
    <section id="privacy" class="section frame" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
      <div class="craft-grid"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Personal stays personal</p><h2 id="privacy-title">Your files.<br/>Your Mac. Your choice.</h2></div><div class="privacy-copy"><p>Files are created and converted locally. No accounts, analytics or app-operated cloud service. CloakTools doesn’t save a browsing history or prefetch your links.</p><p>You choose where files go and which app receives a link. Cloud-managed folders and destination apps follow their own policies.</p><a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">Read the privacy policy <Icon name="link" size={16}/></a></div></div>
    </section>
    <section id="download" class="section frame" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="download-title">
      <div class="download-grid"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Yours to keep</p><h2 id="download-title">Make room for<br/>the little things.</h2><p>macOS 27 or later · Apple silicon only<br/>Free · Public beta 0.6.0</p><a class="air-button air-button--primary" href="https://github.com/cloakyard/cloaktools/releases/download/v0.6.0-beta.20261118.2/CloakTools-v0.6.0-beta.20261118.2.dmg">Download the beta DMG <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a><p class="detail release-note">Build 20261118.2. <a href="https://github.com/cloakyard/cloaktools/releases/tag/v0.6.0-beta.20261118.2">Release notes and checksums</a>.</p></div><div class="install" aria-labelledby="install-title"><h3 id="install-title">On your Mac in a few steps.</h3><ol><li>Open the DMG, drag <strong>CloakTools</strong> to Applications, then launch it there. See the <a href="/install/">installation guide</a>.</li><li>Launch the app, then enable <strong>CloakTools Finder</strong> and open the Finder workspace.</li><li>Create a file, prepare a copy, or try Test a Link in Open With before adding your own rules.</li></ol><p class="detail">This beta is ad-hoc signed and unnotarized. Check for future updates in Settings → About. Finder menus are scoped to CloakTools Files; selected-item Services work in other accessible folders.</p><p class="detail"><a href="/support/">Get setup help</a> · <a href="/source/">Source and roadmap</a></p></div></div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
